<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 28 September, from 48 BCE to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pompey" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">48 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,073 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pompey is murdered on landing in Egypt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fleeing after Pharsalus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> the Great was stabbed to death as he stepped ashore, on the orders of Ptolemy XIII's advisers. Caesar is said to have wept when shown his rival's head.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/935">935 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,091 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Duke Wenceslaus I of Bohemia is murdered by his brother Boleslaus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wenceslaus I, Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> since 921, was murdered by nobles led by his younger brother Boleslaus, who became duke in his place. The year was probably 935, though 929 is also given.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1066">1066 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William of Normandy lands at Pevensey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William's invasion fleet landed unopposed on the Sussex coast while King Harold was in the north. Just over two weeks later William won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hastings">Battle of Hastings</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1106">1106 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">920 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry I of England defeats and captures Robert Curthose at Tinchebray</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Normandy, King Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> defeated the Norman army of his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a>, Duke of Normandy, and captured him. Robert spent the rest of his life in captivity, and Henry reunited Normandy with England.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tinchebray">Battle of Tinchebray</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1322">1322 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">704 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis IV defeats and captures Frederick the Fair at Mühldorf</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Mühldorf am Inn, Louis IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> defeated and captured his cousin and rival king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-fair">Frederick the Fair</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. It is often described as one of the last great battles of mounted knights fought without firearms.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-muhldorf">Battle of Mühldorf</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1781">1781 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American and French armies begin the siege of Yorktown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington and Rochambeau's forces closed in on Cornwallis at Yorktown, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, while a French fleet blocked escape by sea. Cornwallis surrendered on 19 October, effectively ending the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1928">1928 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">98 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander Fleming notices the mould that leads to penicillin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Back from holiday, Alexander Fleming found a mould killing bacteria on a culture plate in his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> laboratory. Developed into a drug in the 1940s, penicillin opened the antibiotic era.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ferdinand Marcos dies in exile in Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Former Philippine president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-marcos">Ferdinand Marcos</a> died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a>, three years after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/people-power-revolution">People Power Revolution</a> drove him from power. His regime was notorious for martial law and plunder.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 28 September <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henri-de-la-tour-dauvergne-duke-of-bouillon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henri-de-la-tour-dauvergne-duke-of-bouillon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henri de La Tour d'Auvergne, Duke of Bouillon</span><span class="tp">1555–1623</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georges-clemenceau"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georges-clemenceau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georges Clemenceau</span><span class="tp">1841–1929</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 28 September <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-vi-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry VI, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="tp">1165–1197</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gertrude-of-merania"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gertrude-of-merania.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gertrude of Merania</span><span class="tp">c. 1185–1213</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gamal-abdel-nasser.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gamal Abdel Nasser</span><span class="tp">1918–1970</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/romulo-betancourt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/romulo-betancourt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rómulo Betancourt</span><span class="tp">1908–1981</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-marcos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ferdinand-marcos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ferdinand Marcos</span><span class="tp">1917–1989</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pierre-trudeau"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pierre-trudeau.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pierre Trudeau</span><span class="tp">1919–2000</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guillermo-endara"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guillermo-endara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Guillermo Endara</span><span class="tp">1936–2009</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
